{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTyZCWu2Xq3i6BdzLhDe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draw anything, this is how I read the request.\n\n**Question:** which screens does a Fernhouse customer pass through to start a return, and where does the 30 day window end it?\n**Outcome:** a product and support team can follow a return from the order list to the confirmation and see where the window sends a customer to Contact support.\n**Dials:** Balanced detail, Mixed audience, Laptop distance, with the app's own words in the labels.\n\n**Settled by your list:**\n- The order list, order detail with a Start a return button, a list of return reasons, the drop-off point or courier pickup choice and the confirmation with a QR code, all current behavior\n- The 30 day window after delivery, with Contact support after it, current behavior\n\n**Left out:**\n- The free pickup for orders over 100 euros, a proposal under review\n- Anything before the order list or after the confirmation\n\n**Assumed:**\n- **The 30 day check sits after Order detail.** You said the app shows Contact support after 30 days but not on which screen. I read it as one decision after Order detail, with Yes leading to the reasons and No to Contact support. A screenshot of the order detail for an order past 30 days would settle it.\n- **The pickup choice is one screen.** You described one choice between a drop-off point and a courier pickup, so I draw it as one decision with two exits that both reach the confirmation. I do not invent a separate screen for picking a drop-off point or booking a courier, because no source shows one. A screenshot of either would add it.\n- **The look:** the accent goes on the 30 day decision, the one place a return can end early, and the confirmation is the goal. The board has three zones, Find the order, Request the return and Done, and the title is \"Start a return\".\n\n**Outline**, in drawing order:\n1. Intent: which screens does a customer pass through to start a return, and where does the 30 day window end it?\n2. Order list, where the flow starts\n3. Order detail, kept because it holds the Start a return button\n4. Within 30 days after delivery?, the accented decision. No leads to Contact support, the exit drawn below the main row. Yes leads on\n5. Pick a reason\n6. Drop-off or courier pickup?, with a Drop-off point exit and a Courier pickup exit, both ending at the confirmation\n7. Confirmation with QR code, the goal\n\nThat is seven nodes and seven connectors, inside the nine-node budget.\n\n**Framings:**\n- **Happy path with the exit beside it.** One straight line to the confirmation, with Contact support below. It shows how a return starts and where it can stop. I recommend this one.\n- **State map with every exit equal.** It shows more outcomes but pulls the eye off the path, and the sources hold only one exit.\n\n**Still open:** none beyond the two assumed readings above.\n\nIs this the right reading of the board?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3593,"cache_read_input_tokens":89544,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3593},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"77eec16c-adac-48d8-8e00-0d3abd488624","uuid":"8f155d80-8e45-4aa0-ad7f-fc3d2bf131b3","timestamp":"2026-10-28T04:07:23.108Z","request_id":"req_011CgTyZCKFUYi16UraMd9HL"}
